module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalOnCover.LocalGeneration
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorFiniteLocallyFree
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorStalkRingedSpace
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.KFlatResolution
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Finiteness of tensor products of sheaves of modules on a ringed space

Let `(X, 𝒪_X)` be a ringed space and let `F`, `G` be `𝒪_X`-modules. Stacks 01CE asserts that
seven properties of sheaves of modules pass to `F ⊗_{𝒪_X} G`. Three of them are proved here:
local generation by sections, finite type and local freeness, which are clauses (1), (2) and
(7) of the source.

The mathematics is the same as on a ringed site, where it is Stacks 03L6, and that is where it
is proved: a covering of `X` on whose members `F` is generated by sections, intersected with
one for `G`, is a covering on whose members a family of generating sections of the tensor
product is obtained by tensoring the two families, and for a local basis the same construction
gives a local basis indexed by the product of the two index sets. What is done here is to read
those site-level statements at the site of opens of `X` with its open-cover topology, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.ringedSite X`; the tensor product of sheaves of modules on that
ringed site *is* the tensor product `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.tensorSheaf`
of Stacks 01CA that the other four clauses of 01CE are stated for, so the statements below are
about one tensor product and the seven clauses compose.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorSheaf_nonempty_localGeneratorsData`: **Stacks 01CE
  (1).** If `F` and `G` are locally generated by sections, so is `F ⊗_{𝒪_X} G`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorSheaf_isFiniteType`: **Stacks 01CE (2).** If `F` and
  `G` are of finite type, so is `F ⊗_{𝒪_X} G`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorSheaf_isLocallyFree`: **Stacks 01CE (7).** If `F` and
  `G` are locally free, so is `F ⊗_{𝒪_X} G`.

The remaining four clauses are `AlgebraicGeometry.tensorSheaf_isQuasicoherent` (3),
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorSheaf_isFinitePresentation` (4),
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorSheaf_isCoherent_of_isFinitePresentation` (5) and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorSheaf_isCoherent` (6).

## Implementation notes

**Which predicate says "locally generated by sections", and which says "locally free".** On a
ringed site the source's conditions are the predicates of Stacks 03DL,
`SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite` and `SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFreeOnSite`,
each of which quantifies over every object of the site. On a ringed space the conditions are
instead about the space itself: an open covering of `X` on each member of which the restriction
is generated by global sections, respectively is free. That is exactly Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.LocalGeneratorsData` — a covering of the terminal object together with
generating sections of each restriction — and, with the generating sections required to be
bases, Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFree`, which carries Stacks 01C6 (1). Those are the
predicates used below, so that the statements read as the source does and match the way the
rest of the development states the two conditions for a ringed space (for instance
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.modulePullback_nonempty_localGeneratorsData` for Stacks 01B3). For
clause (1) the passage between the two readings is Stacks 03DN,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_coversTop` in one direction and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_exists_cover_generatingSections`
in the other; for clause (7) no passage is needed, because
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataTensor` already builds the local basis of the tensor
product out of local bases of the factors.

**Two spellings of the structure sheaf as a sheaf of rings.**
`(AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.ringedSite X).ringSheaf` and
`structureSheafRing X` are equal by `rfl`, and so
are the two tensor products formed over them, but the first reaches the second only by
unfolding `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose`, which instance search does not do: it runs at
reducible transparency. So each finiteness hypothesis is restated at the ringed-site spelling
by `assumption`, which checks the two against each other at default transparency, before the
site-level theorem is applied.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03L6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03L6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C6)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules

variable (X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u})
  (F G : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))

/-- Finite type over `structureSheafRing X` is finite type over the ringed-site spelling. -/
private theorem isFiniteType_ringSheaf_ringedSite [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F] :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u}
      (R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.ringedSite X).O)
      F := by assumption

/-- Local freeness over `structureSheafRing X` is local freeness over the ringed-site spelling. -/
private theorem isLocallyFree_ringSheaf_ringedSite
    [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFree.{u, u, u} F] :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFree.{u, u, u}
      (R := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.ringedSite X).O)
      F := by assumption

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01CE (1).** On a ringed space, the tensor product of two sheaves of
modules which are locally generated by sections is locally generated by sections: there is an
open covering of `X` on each member of which `F ⊗_{𝒪_X} G` is generated by global sections.

This is Stacks 03L6 for local generation by sections,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties.tensorSheaf_isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite`,
read at the site of opens of `X`, with Stacks 03DN moving between the covering of `X` that the
statement speaks of and the condition at every open that the site-level predicate asserts. -/
@[stacks 01CE "tensor_locally_generated"]
theorem tensorSheaf_nonempty_localGeneratorsData
    (hF : Nonempty F.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u})
    (hG : Nonempty G.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u}) :
    Nonempty ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor
      ⟨((X)).presheaf, ((X)).IsSheaf⟩).obj (F)).obj (G))).LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u} := by
  obtain ⟨qF⟩ := hF
  obtain ⟨qG⟩ := hG
  have h :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties.tensorSheaf_isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite
      (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.ringedSite X) F G
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_coversTop F qF.X qF.coversTop
        fun i => ⟨qF.generators i⟩)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_coversTop G qG.X qG.coversTop
        fun i => ⟨qG.generators i⟩)
  obtain ⟨I, U, hU, hgen⟩ :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_iff_exists_cover_generatingSections
      (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.ringedSite X) _).1 h
  exact ⟨{ I := I, X := U, coversTop := hU, generators := fun i => (hgen i).some }⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01CE (2).** On a ringed space, the tensor product of two sheaves of
modules of finite type is of finite type.

This is Stacks 03L6 for the finite type condition,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties.tensorSheaf_isFiniteType`, read at the site of
opens of `X`; the predicate is the same one on both sides, since Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` already asks for a covering of the space. -/
@[stacks 01CE "tensor_finite_type", instance]
theorem tensorSheaf_isFiniteType [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F]
    [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} G] :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u}
      ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor
        ⟨((X)).presheaf, ((X)).IsSheaf⟩).obj (F)).obj (G))) := by
  have := isFiniteType_ringSheaf_ringedSite X F
  have := isFiniteType_ringSheaf_ringedSite X G
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorLocalProperties.tensorSheaf_isFiniteType
    (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.ringedSite X) F G

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01CE (7).** On a ringed space, the tensor product of two locally free
sheaves of modules is locally free.

Following the source: on a member of a covering trivializing both factors, `F` is free on a
basis `B_F` and `G` on a basis `B_G`, and the tensor product is free on `B_F × B_G`. The local
basis is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataTensor`, which is built on the common
refinement of the two given coverings, and its members are bases by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyFreeData_localGeneratorsDataTensor`. -/
@[stacks 01CE "tensor_locally_free", instance]
theorem tensorSheaf_isLocallyFree [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFree.{u, u, u} F]
    [_root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFree.{u, u, u} G] :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFree.{u, u, u}
      ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor
        ⟨((X)).presheaf, ((X)).IsSheaf⟩).obj (F)).obj (G))) := by
  obtain ⟨qF, hqF⟩ := (isLocallyFree_ringSheaf_ringedSite X F).exists_isLocallyFreeData
  obtain ⟨qG, hqG⟩ := (isLocallyFree_ringSheaf_ringedSite X G).exists_isLocallyFreeData
  have := Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyFreeData_localGeneratorsDataTensor X.sheaf qF qG
  exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataTensor X.sheaf qF qG).isLocallyFree

end AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules

end
